## Linux Storage Management (LVM)

### Initial Configuration

The Ubuntu Server VM was provisioned with a 40 GiB
virtual disk. However, the default guided LVM
installation allocated only 19 GiB to the root
logical volume.

### Investigation

The following commands were used to inspect
disk and LVM allocation:

- `lsblk`
- `df -h`
- `sudo pvs`
- `sudo vgs`
- `sudo lvs`

The investigation identified 19 GiB of unallocated
space within the ubuntu-vg volume group.

### Resolution

Extended the root logical volume and resized
the filesystem using:

    sudo lvextend -l +100%FREE -r /dev/ubuntu-vg/ubuntu-lv

### Skills Demonstrated

- Linux filesystem management
- Logical Volume Manager (LVM)
- Storage capacity analysis
- Logical volume expansion
- Online filesystem resizing
- Command-line administration
